","merged_at":null},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13803.\r\n\r\nImplemented as a proof-of-concept, though the code should be good to merge as-is. ~~Except for the fact that it doesn't yet have documentation or unit tests.~~\r\n\r\nThis adds a simple `@export_suffix` annotation that takes a string argument as a suffix (similar to the `suffix:` hint). It's implemented mostly the same as `@export_range`, but without the whole range part. It can be applied to ints, floats and vectors. It also accepts additional arguments as extra hints.\r\n\r\nI also noticed that `_parse_range_hint` gets called for some other variant types, such as quaternions and transforms, but I don't think changing the suffix/unit in those cases would make sense, so I left those out.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nExample from one of my projects:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1529\" height=\"645\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/96a2dd5e-0b2a-4cca-9b5a-33445a0c579c\" />\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113839/reactions","total_count":21,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":10,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113839/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}